{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3958-can-someone-talk-about-krewe-mythos","id":3958,"title":"Can someone talk about Krewe mythos?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-05T19:49:14-08:00","id":3958,"title":"Can someone talk about Krewe mythos?","content":"I kind of want to get a better idea of GtSI and the Krewe Mythos seems like a good place to start because they are pretty weird. It seems really weird that the players are supposed to come up with some elaborate explanation for reality that doesn't match reality that well. Not only that the book can give the impression that joining the Krewe invalidates the work you put into your Geist before joining as the Geist is overridden by the aspect. I know this is not supposed to be the case but the sample characters in the book only have the Aspect listed without the original Geist and the example of Krewe Mythos creation mentions a Geist claiming that he was lying before about his identity because his host wasn't cool enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/801-grytorm","name":"Grytorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T08:49:08-08:00","id":4368,"title":"","content":"I've recently finished writing the new version for my Geist Chronicles fanbook so this is fresh on my mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> The first thing is that this<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3958-can-someone-talk-about-krewe-mythos#post3958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> that the players are supposed to come up with some elaborate explanation for reality that doesn't match reality that well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Is wrong.<br /> <br /> Now Sin-Eaters don't know how reality works. In the WoD no one knows how reality works. However their Krewe Mythos is supposed to be as accurate as Sin-Eaters can make it. No Sin-Eater will ever come up with a mythology that says Ghosts don't exist. <br /> <br /> <br /> Rather a Mythology is about explaining things. Why do Ghosts linger, why does the underworld exist, why isn't there a kindly Grim Reaper who rides up and helps every last Ghost Pass On to it's just fate?<br /> <br /> Every game has questions that can never be answered. What really happened to Father Wolf? Who were the Oracles? In Geist these questions are the sort of thing your Krewe Mythology answers. And Sin-Eaters know their answers tend to be made up or stolen from Harry Potter. Most of the time a Krew's myth is an excuse to walk around with badass symbols on your t-shirt. The rest of the time, well there's not much solid evidence in God. It's about faith instead of proof.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grytorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/3958-can-someone-talk-about-krewe-mythos#post3958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not only that the book can give the impression that joining the Krewe invalidates the work you put into your Geist before joining as the Geist is overridden by the aspect.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah; that section really just needed more details on the possibilities of how an Aspect could manifest; including ones where nothing really changes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:26:43-08:00","id":4406,"title":"","content":"Where is this fanbook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T12:54:18-08:00","id":4532,"title":"","content":"About 30% done, you'll have to wait I'm afraid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T13:53:45-08:00","id":4571,"title":"","content":"No one has canonical answers about how the World of Darkness works - the writers try hard to keep it that way. But Sin Eaters are both worse off and more personalized than most splats because they don't come with a widely spanning cultures, with ancient traditions and myths regarding what they are or what they're supposed to do. Instead, they have Krewe mythos, which, in the eyes of the characters, is a revelation from the Underworld about why the world exists the way it does. Out of character, this revelation is created from the characters' (and their geists') experiences and innermost beliefs, all meshed together. The result is that their personal myth actually explains reality perfectly - from the character's experiences.<br /> <br /> The geists do take on archetypal roles from this revelation, but it doesn't exactly override their original concept. It's supposed to expand on the original concept and make it more <i>mythic</i>. With this in mind, I usually come up with possibilities for the mythic aspect when I design the geist - and what kind of beliefs my character will contribute.<br /> <br /> It's an odd system of doing things, and it's not presently very clearly in the core, but its supposed to make 'the truth' much more personalized to the characters and the game. Rather than hearing about &quot;Father Wolf,&quot; which might not mean anything to the characters, they hear a story which confirms their beliefs and fears.<br /> <br /> [addition]: Naturally, these myths are tested when they experience something unexplained, or when they hear a contradicting story from another krewe... but doesn't that make interesting conflict? I imagine that very few characters will simply lose faith and call their myth a fabrication just because their rivals down the block said they heard something different. Maybe the more secular Sin-Eaters will investigate these inconsistencies and find the reason why they exist and what's true. Some will deny these other myths are true, or fight to prove their own. Many will probably feel confident enough in how well their myth matches their understanding, and let it lie. Those responses can inspire interesting and dramatic stories.<br /> <br /> At least that's what I think they were going for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":". 11-06-2013, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T14:12:21-08:00","id":4581,"title":"","content":"That sounds like what they were trying for; though I always felt that revelation aspect was a little... questionable. On the one hand I recently had some ideas about how Geist Aspects could work which I am really pleased with <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T10:33:10-08:00","id":6907,"title":"","content":"Any ideas on what &quot;mythology&quot; a Krewe with 3 charakters (with different primary priority on metal/social/pyhical attributes and skills) could be?<br /> Something like &quot;three belog together cause they function like a trinity blah&quot; possible?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/709-nihil","name":"Nihil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar709_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T11:13:03-08:00","id":6935,"title":"","content":"I'm imagining a krewe that firmly believes in the cosmology presented in Wraith, and everyone else thinks they are idiots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T13:30:02-08:00","id":7002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_con